Package: ducky-can-shoot
Version: @VERSION@-@REVISION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Linux-Alex <alex.marinic22@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Linux-Alex/ducky-can-shoot
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/Linux-Alex/ducky-can-shoot.git
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-pyqt6 (>= 6.5),
 python3-pyqt6.qtqml,
 python3-pyqt6.qtquick,
 python3-requests,
 qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
 qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
 qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
 qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
 qml6-module-qtquick-templates,
 qml6-module-qtqml-workerscript,
 libqt6svg6,
 qt6-svg-plugins,
 libglib2.0-bin,
 zip,
 udisks2,
 util-linux
Recommends: clamav, clamav-daemon, clamav-freshclam, p7zip-full, libnotify-bin
Description: USB malware triage: scan, archive, upload and notify
 Ducky Can Shoot triages removable media: it scans every file on a USB stick with
 ClamAV and a built-in heuristic engine, archives the medium into one image,
 uploads that image to a free host and emails the verdict, with the download link
 when the medium is safe.
 .
 If a threat is found, nothing is archived and nothing is uploaded, so malware
 never leaves the machine that owns the medium.  The interface is Qt Quick with
 Kirigami; the same pipeline is available as the dcs command.
